Whilst this makes sense, it also brings back the performance issues and also why I removed the anchor node in my PR to begin with, especially for the common case of:

```svelte
{#each items as item}
  {@render children(item)}
{/each}
```

The extra comment node makes large lists much slower during unmount.

I assume that optimisation is true for this too?

```svelte
{#each things as thing}
  <div>{…}</div>
{/each}
```

That was already the case. [See for yourself](https://svelte-5-preview-fzjdomutm-svelte.vercel.app/#H4sIAAAAAAAAEyWLQQqAIBBFryLTNmwvEnSOaiE55YCZNBaEePeSdu993s-wkkcGNWYIZkdQMMQILaQnVuEbfcLP-bjOpS65QbM4kRyFjYXhn8oUhNCW7l5KqbsKU8hdTcv33g9LK6EFlc4Ly1xeZf0xw3gAAAA=):

```js
$.each(node, 1, () => things, $.index, ($$anchor, thing, $$index) => {
  var div = root_1();

  $.append($$anchor, div);
});
```
